    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0263" n="997" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg997"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Butler to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s 45, of 8th instant. Forsee here and located Chester
                    Rowe. Latter assumed Mexican nationality by purchase real estate, thus protected
                    from extradition. See article 6 extradition treaty, article 30 Mexican federal
                    constitution, and article 1, section 10, law on foreigners, reported by
                    legation’s 241, June 10, 1886. Please instruct me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
